            "text": "Rate-limit bypass in public contact endpoint via spoofed forwarding headers\n\nThe public **`/api/contact`** endpoint derives its rate-limit key from client-supplied forwarding headers, allowing an unauthenticated attacker to evade the intended spam throttle by changing **`X-Forwarded-For`** or **`X-Real-IP`** values. This keeps attacker-controlled requests flowing into the service-role-backed contact ingestion path despite the presence of a limiter."
          },
          "locations": [
