              "description": {
                "text": "1. Derive the rate-limit key from a server-trusted client address provided by the runtime or hosting platform, not from raw request headers.\n2. For Astro server routes, prefer the framework-provided client address value and fall back to a safe sentinel when it is unavailable.\n3. Treat **`X-Forwarded-For`** and **`X-Real-IP`** as untrusted unless they have been sanitized by a specifically trusted reverse proxy under application control.\n4. Apply the same rule consistently anywhere the shared IP helper is used for security decisions, including other throttled endpoints.",
                "markdown": "1. Derive the rate-limit key from a server-trusted client address provided by the runtime or hosting platform, not from raw request headers.\n2. For Astro server routes, prefer the framework-provided client address value and fall back to a safe sentinel when it is unavailable.\n3. Treat **`X-Forwarded-For`** and **`X-Real-IP`** as untrusted unless they have been sanitized by a specifically trusted reverse proxy under application control.\n4. Apply the same rule consistently anywhere the shared IP helper is used for security decisions, including other throttled endpoints."
